WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.001
-Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:03.836
I am here with John Oliver,
the host of

00:00:03.836 --> 00:00:05.605
"Last Week Tonight with
John Oliver."

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.374
I always love having you
on the show.

00:00:07.374 --> 00:00:10.677
And thank you for doing
"Hey Robot."

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:11.911
-Of course.

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:15.648
I was going to say "a pleasure,"
but it wasn't.

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:17.016
It wasn't.

00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:21.487
I really hope, Jimmy, you didn't
cut out my question about

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:23.857
what union busting is.

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:27.193
I presume you left that in.

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:30.630
-I was just on -- I was just
going to take your joke again.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:34.100
I was just on grumpycat.com.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.869
I kind of remember Grumpy Cat
was like a --

00:00:36.869 --> 00:00:40.306
It was a cat, right?
It looked sad?

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:43.709
-Yeah. Do you know what?
We tried to get Grumpy Cat.

00:00:43.709 --> 00:00:46.980
In the first year, I think,
of our show,

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.248
we had an idea for a joke
and we said --

00:00:49.248 --> 00:00:51.051
We got in touch with
Grumpy Cat's people,

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:52.785
saying,
"Could we have Grumpy Cat?"

00:00:52.785 --> 00:00:56.989
They sent back the --
the first-class plane tickets

00:00:56.989 --> 00:00:59.159
they would need
and what Grumpy Cat cost,

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:01.027
and we thought,
"[Bleep] Grumpy Cat.

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:03.329
We don't need that
for this joke."

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:07.466
I'll tell you what we can get.
Another cat.

00:01:07.466 --> 00:01:12.405
-We did something -- We had a
dog that was a famous dog

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:13.906
that didn't --
It just looked cute.

00:01:13.906 --> 00:01:15.074
It didn't do anything.

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:18.244
It just sat on a dog bed
and looked cute.

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:21.581
And it was --
Oh, no, I'm so sorry.

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:26.085
It was backstage at
a Kevin Hart concert.

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:27.887
-Wow!
-I swear to God.

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:31.724
-You are fully conflating
two memories there.

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:32.892
"Was it on the show?

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:34.727
"It was backstage at
a Kevin Hart concert.

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:38.431
You know what? I dreamt it.
Let's move on."

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:41.000
Wait. No, I --
We have to go back.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.704
You saw a famous dog lying
on a bed backstage

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:45.872
at a Kevin Hart concert?

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:49.175
-Yes.
I went to a Kevin Hart concert.

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:52.745
I went backstage,
and in a room, they go,

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:55.215
"Do you want to meet..."
something dog or something.

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:57.483
And I go,
"I have no idea what that is.

00:01:57.483 --> 00:02:00.453
I'm just here -- I'm gonna
say hi to Kevin, and then..."

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:02.989
They go,
"Well, the owners would like

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:05.157
you to say hello to"
whatever it was.

00:02:05.157 --> 00:02:06.559
And so I went in,

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:09.862
and there was like a line of
people waiting to meet this dog.

00:02:09.862 --> 00:02:11.497
The dog was in
one of the rooms backstage,

00:02:11.497 --> 00:02:12.899
like had his own dressing room.

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:16.602
-I mean, every anecdote from
before the pandemic

00:02:16.602 --> 00:02:18.605
seems dislocating now.

00:02:18.605 --> 00:02:20.406
To me, that's one of
the weirdest anecdotes

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:21.607
I've ever heard.

00:02:21.607 --> 00:02:23.843
I feel like you've thrown
that out, Jimmy,

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:25.445
like that's
a normal thing to say.

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:28.748
"I met this famous dog backstage
of a Kevin Hart concert"

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:31.551
is a sequence of words in
the English language

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:35.821
I don't think have ever
been said before.

00:02:35.821 --> 00:02:37.423
-Oh, my gosh.

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:40.593
-"I met this
famous dog backstage

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:45.297
at a Kevin Hart concert,
and it looked disappointed.

00:02:45.297 --> 00:02:46.532
And I kind of got it."

00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:48.134
-I want to talk about
some topical things,

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:49.602
if you don't mind.

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:51.971
Something everyone has been
talking about this past week is

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:54.974
Prince Harry and Meghan's
interview with Oprah.

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:58.711
-Right.
-Did you watch this?

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:01.647
-I did. I did watch it.
-The whole thing?

00:03:01.647 --> 00:03:05.284
-Yeah, my wife was -- She --
I watched it soup to nuts,

00:03:05.284 --> 00:03:06.786
the whole thing.

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:10.156
And, yeah, it was --
It was amazing?

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:12.992
I mean, I will say, I didn't
find any of it surprising.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:16.495
That was kind of what
I felt like, sadly,

00:03:16.495 --> 00:03:17.963
her experience was
going to be going in,

00:03:17.963 --> 00:03:19.265
because, you know, I grew up --

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:22.134
I know the royal family
from a distance,

00:03:22.134 --> 00:03:24.871
and they seemed like
flawed people.

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:27.940
That's literally the kindest way
I could possibly put it.

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:30.309
-Nothing shocked you at all
about the interview?

00:03:30.309 --> 00:03:33.813
-The only thing that shocked me
afterwards was that

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:35.215
Oprah, the next day,
saying, "Oh, Prince Harry

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:37.016
wants to make it clear
that it wasn't

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:39.919
Prince Philip being racist,"
which made me think, "Really?

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:42.321
Okay, that -- that is
actually surprising."

00:03:42.321 --> 00:03:43.489
I think was assumed,

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:45.925
And I guess people
just didn't hear him.

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:49.228
-Do you think any change
will come from this interview?

00:03:49.228 --> 00:03:51.631
-I don't -- I mean,
it's hard to say, isn't it?

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:54.500
Because the royal family --

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.670
its whole selling point
is that it doesn't change.

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:59.805
That was kind of the point of it
over centuries,

00:03:59.805 --> 00:04:02.174
that, you know,
times come and go,

00:04:02.174 --> 00:04:04.510
governments rise and fall,
but the royal family

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.713
will always be there,
unyielding,

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:09.081
the stiff upper lip that
doesn't wobble.

00:04:09.081 --> 00:04:11.784
So that's their selling point.

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:15.922
As years go by,
you realize that not changing

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:20.192
is not entirely a good thing,
because that means

00:04:20.192 --> 00:04:21.427
the times might be
changing around you,

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:23.463
and you are refusing to evolve.

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:25.398
So I don't think
they will change,

00:04:25.398 --> 00:04:27.299
because I don't think they
have the capacity to,

00:04:27.299 --> 00:04:28.634
but they obviously should.

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:30.302
The one person who I think
has been really happy

00:04:30.302 --> 00:04:31.837
about all of this is
Prince Andrew.

00:04:31.837 --> 00:04:34.773
I'm guessing that
he has been nudging

00:04:34.773 --> 00:04:37.743
the royal family like, "Can you
believe what Meghan did, huh?

00:04:37.743 --> 00:04:39.145
Can you believe it?

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:41.947
Dragging this family's name
into disrepute,

00:04:41.947 --> 00:04:43.149
shaming us, right?"

00:04:43.149 --> 00:04:46.251
-"Everyone is talking about this
and only this."

00:04:46.251 --> 00:04:50.590
-"She's ruined our reputation.
She has, right, guys?"

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:52.525
Wow.
-Wow.

00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:55.260
The other week on your show,
you briefly talked about

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:57.763
Ted Cruz going to Cancun.

00:04:57.763 --> 00:05:00.632
And I got the feeling that there
was more you wanted to say

00:05:00.632 --> 00:05:03.269
but didn't have the time.

00:05:03.269 --> 00:05:04.637
We have the time now.
Is there --

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:11.044
-Oh, I mean, the thing that
was most tantalizing to me

00:05:11.044 --> 00:05:13.813
about that regretful episode

00:05:13.813 --> 00:05:17.015
was Heidi Cruz's
group chat leaking,

00:05:17.015 --> 00:05:20.919
Because I think it just
really drilled home to me

00:05:20.919 --> 00:05:23.889
that nothing good
comes from a group chat.

00:05:23.889 --> 00:05:25.357
I don't mess with
group chats, Jimmy.

00:05:25.357 --> 00:05:27.526
-I wonder if she found out
which friend it was.

00:05:27.526 --> 00:05:29.595
-Oh, she definitely found out
which friend it was.

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:31.330
I think she knew going in.

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:33.799
You know what the weak link
in a group chat is.

00:05:33.799 --> 00:05:35.868
She knows --
She didn't need to find out.

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:37.403
She knew.

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:40.373
-Do you think there's
another group chat

00:05:40.373 --> 00:05:42.441
that's talking about Heidi Cruz?

00:05:42.441 --> 00:05:46.211
-Oh, 100%. There is absolutely.

00:05:46.211 --> 00:05:47.813
The group chat with
Heidi Cruz on it,

00:05:47.813 --> 00:05:51.016
and then there's the same group
chat without Heidi Cruz on it.

00:05:51.016 --> 00:05:55.387
And that is the group chat
that I want to see.

00:05:55.387 --> 00:05:57.723
I want to see the
"Can you believe this [bleep]"

00:05:57.723 --> 00:06:01.126
from the rest of the neighbors.

00:06:01.126 --> 00:06:03.829
That's the group chat
with the good stuff in.

00:06:03.829 --> 00:06:06.131
That is the one group chat
I will join.

00:06:06.131 --> 00:06:07.633
-Yeah. Oh, really? Okay.

00:06:07.633 --> 00:06:10.236
-Heidi Cruz's neighbors's
group chat that she's not on.

00:06:10.236 --> 00:06:13.605
That. Invite me. I'm there.

00:06:13.605 --> 00:06:16.475
-This past year has been
tough for a lot of people.

00:06:16.475 --> 00:06:19.645
And I just want to say one thing
I love about your show

00:06:19.645 --> 00:06:23.448
is that you're continuously
finding ways to give and donate.

00:06:23.448 --> 00:06:28.320
And you donate in
interesting ways to food banks.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:31.391
-I think what we were really
doing is kind of

00:06:31.391 --> 00:06:33.425
money-laundering
HBO's production budget

00:06:33.425 --> 00:06:35.261
to food banks
over the last year.

00:06:35.261 --> 00:06:37.897
So it felt like
we were just -- each week,

00:06:37.897 --> 00:06:39.231
we were trying to come up
with different ways

00:06:39.231 --> 00:06:41.434
to kind of force a donation
to a food bank.

00:06:41.434 --> 00:06:43.402
"No, sell us this painting.

00:06:43.402 --> 00:06:47.573
We'll give you --
Name your sewage plant after me.

00:06:47.573 --> 00:06:49.508
Give it to a food bank."
-That was the best.

00:06:49.508 --> 00:06:52.078
The sewage plant was the best.

00:06:52.078 --> 00:06:53.712
So, wait.
So, you just go like this.

00:06:53.712 --> 00:06:54.847
"We're just making a show.

00:06:54.847 --> 00:06:55.981
We needed a budget for that,

00:06:55.981 --> 00:06:57.216
and the money will go
to the food bank."

00:06:57.216 --> 00:06:58.450
-Yeah, that's right.

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:01.520
"You've given us this money,
HBO, for a reason.

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:03.422
We're gonna use it
for something else now."

00:07:03.422 --> 00:07:05.758
Is that the definition of fraud?

00:07:05.758 --> 00:07:10.096
Seems to be, but let's
just assume that charity

00:07:10.096 --> 00:07:12.264
has happened
and not an actual crime.

00:07:12.264 --> 00:07:15.000
-That's a better way to put it.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:17.035
John, we love everything
you're doing.

00:07:17.035 --> 00:07:19.805
We always -- I personally,
I love every single time

00:07:19.805 --> 00:07:22.107
you come on, and thank you
for being so funny

00:07:22.107 --> 00:07:24.309
and for doing those shows
and just getting us through

00:07:24.309 --> 00:07:27.947
the trickiest political times
and making us all laugh.

00:07:27.947 --> 00:07:30.982
Really, it doesn't fall on
deaf ears.

00:07:30.982 --> 00:07:33.052
-I appreciate it, mate. Thanks.
-John Oliver, everybody.

00:07:33.052 --> 00:07:34.453
"Last Week Tonight with
John Oliver"

00:07:34.453 --> 00:07:37.056
airs Sundays at 11:00 p.m.
on HBO.

